From 4cf94b2fd0979283c09eae9d93733ad48328f3c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 17:30:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] PCI: cadence: sky1-cix: restore ACPI native mode on v7.3
 (0027 remainder + 0029)

Native Sky1 PCIe (sky1_pcie_native, the default when the cmdline does not
say sky1_pcie_native=off) could not work on the v7.3-rc5 port. There were
three independent defects:

1. Driver name clash. Mainline pci-sky1.c (CONFIG_PCI_SKY1_HOST=y) and the
   CIX vendor driver both registered "sky1-pcie". pci-sky1.o links first,
   so the vendor driver failed with "already registered" and nothing
   drove CIXH2020. The vendor driver is renamed "sky1-pcie-cix" again, as
   7.2 patch 0027 did; binding is by its ACPI match table.
2. Wrong root-port window and a type-confused capability walk. The port
   read the LGA root-port base CDNS_PCIE_RP_BASE (0x200000) on this HPA
   controller, and passed an __iomem window to cdns_pcie_find_capability(),
   which since v7.x takes a struct cdns_pcie *. A void * converts
   silently, so the walk dereferenced MMIO as a struct. This restores
   CDNS_PCIE_HPA_RP_BASE and the BSP-style
   sky1_cdns_pcie_find_{,ext_}capability() helpers (read functions made
   static).
3. The HPA host path never programmed the ECAM outbound region. The port
   restores cdns_pcie_hpa_create_region_for_ecam() from 0027 and gates it
   on the new rc->sky1_bsp_ecam_region, which only the vendor driver sets,
   so the mainline DT driver's path is unchanged. It also restores the
   ACPI/_DSD "vendor-id", "device-id" and "cdns,no-inbound-bar"
   properties, and device_property_read_u32() for
   "cdns,no-bar-match-nbits" (DT callers see no change).

Also restores 0029: under ACPI, the axi/apb/refclk_b clocks come from the
CLKT clkdev entries keyed by acpi_dev_name(), which clk-sky1-acpi.c
already registers in this tree. They are released by devm actions.

The default cmdline (sky1_pcie_native=off pcie_pnp_en) is unaffected. In
that mode pci-sky1-acpi blocks CIXH2020 and the firmware ECAM host drives
PCIe. Native mode stays hardware-unverified. The r279 boot sheet gates it
separately.

Source parity: pci-sky1-cix.c, pci-sky1-debugfs.c, the capability helpers
and the HPA ECAM function are the r277 (v7.2.8, hardware-validated) code
adapted to the v7.3 cadence core. The register offsets keep mainline
pci-sky1.c's values.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [oe-specific]
Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
